= Times are changing

Following the invasion of <span style="color: [+ ukraine_color_1 +];">**Ukra**</span><span style="color: [+ ukraine_color_2 +];">**ine**</span>, Chancellor Olaf Scholz held a speech in the Bundestag condemning the previous military policy of the <span style="color: [+ spd_color +];">Schröder</span>-<span style="color: [+ cdu_color +];">Merkel</span> era. Defining the war as a "historical turning point", Scholz has called for an enormous increase in military expenditure amounting to 100 billion €. This is a sharp break from the pacifist line of the old <span style="color: [+ spd_color +];">SPD</span>, but his this increased militarisation popular all across the political spectrum, even earning the praise of <span style="color: [+ cdu_color +];">**CDU**</span> opposition leader [+ cdu_leader +].

What should our reaction be?

